        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nTHEODORE B. OLSON, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nIAN HEATH GERSHENGORN, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent.\nEDWIN S. KNEEDLER, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Mr. Olson, may I ask you to go one step beyond that on an issue of fact that I just don't understand from reading the briefs? Let me give you three quick quotations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Well, what event triggers, if you will, the incidence of the tax on the distributor?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Olson",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statute explicitly says, Justice O'Connor -- this is on page 2 of the petition -- the incidence of this tax is imposed on the distributor of the first receipt of the motor fuel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What does -- what does that mean, that the tax is imposed on the use, sale, or delivery?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does that mean, Mr. Olson, that the tax that the -- the fuel, rather, that's sold to the United States Government, later, out-of-State, when is the credit for the sales out-of-State made? Is that made at the time of the initial delivery, or is -- do they ask for a refund a month later?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statute says, in 3408, \"a tax per gallon is hereby imposed on the use, sale, or delivery of fuel.\" It does not say \"the receipt of fuel.\" \"The distributor\" is defined as somebody who receives and uses, sells, or delivers fuel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\"what\" is in -- is in 79-3408(a), and it is clearly imposed on the use, sale, or delivery of the fuel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What if -- what -- perhaps the State expresses it that way just to cover some people who get their gas illegally, and they would say the tax is still due, even if you haven't gotten your gas from a distributor who has paid the State tax. Wouldn't that suffice for why the court imposes the tax on the use, sale, or delivery? Use, sale, or delivery."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "it, or deliver it. And if the distributor -- if the distributor is -- hasn't done one of those things, then it's -- then it -- then the distributor can be made liable for any tax increases that have -- that happen while the distributor is holding the tax."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is the commerce constitutionally -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is it relevant -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The fatality rate is four times the national average. And the tribe is using those revenues to fix -- advance that particular Federal interest, which is reflected in Federal statutes and in the Federal regulatory scheme."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF KNEEDLER ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think the court was wrong to conclude that the incidence was on the -- was on the distributor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But none of this -- none of this mattered to the tenth circuit, though, did it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Section 3401(f)(3), it defines a \"distributor\" as someone who receives the product."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-631",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2758705f73bbccf0c1767089e7cb88e2be87d16b3a1ea278037c3af8a6bdfd8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2758705f73bb-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Aren't there usually two incidents? You talk about the incident of the taxes on a person, but it's also on an event."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
